    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just the apartment though. it's like the person who lived here is actually gone. ten years of my life was just... tied to them. now i wake up and i don't even know what i'm supposed to do with my hands or my time. i feel like a ghost just drifting through the motions. it's exhausting trying to act like a person when there's nothing left inside.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes sense that the silence of the apartment now feels like a silence for a self that no longer feels you exist. When a decade of life is tied to a person and that person is gone, it is very easy to feel like you are just a ghost in a life you no longer own.\n\nIt is okay to stop pretending to \"live\" for a while and just rest in the exhaustion of that gap.",
